[Event "NF-001 - Knight royal fork: immediate check on d6"]
[Site "Original teaching position"]
[Date "2026.09.05"]
[Round "9"]
[White "White to move"]
[Black "Win the queen"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "2q1k3/8/8/8/2N5/8/8/6K1 w - - 0 1"]
[Pattern "Multiple threats > Fork > Knight > King and queen > Immediate checking fork"]

{Find a checking fork that wins the queen. This is a pattern exercise, not a unique engine-best-move claim.}
1. Nd6+ {The knight attacks e8 and c8. Black cannot block a knight check and neither the king nor queen can capture d6.}
1... Kf8 (1... Kd8 2. Nxc8) (1... Kd7 2. Nxc8) (1... Ke7 2. Nxc8)
2. Nxc8 {The exact same fork works against every legal response.} *

[Event "WM-001 - Windmill: capture, return with check, capture again"]
[Site "Original teaching position"]
[Date "2026.09.05"]
[Round "10"]
[White "White to move"]
[Black "Demonstrate two windmill captures"]
[Result "*"]
[SetUp "1"]
[FEN "5r1k/5bRp/5B2/8/8/3B4/8/1K6 w - - 0 1"]
[Pattern "Named combinations > Windmill > Rook discovers bishop check"]

{Learning demonstration: capture h7, return with check, then capture f7. There are alternative captures and winning moves; this line is selected to teach the mechanism.}
1. Rxh7+ {The rook takes a pawn and uncovers Bf6-h8. Bd3 protects h7, preventing Kxh7.}
1... Kg8 {Only legal move.}
2. Rg7+ {A direct rook check restores the starting mechanism.}
2... Kh8 {Only legal move.}
3. Rxf7+ {The rook harvests the bishop while uncovering another check.}
3... Kg8 {Only legal move.}
4. Rg7+ Kh8 {The cycle is restored. White has gained a pawn and bishop. This is a mechanism demonstration rather than a shortest-win puzzle.} *
